## Summary
===============================================================================

- You can use, copy, and integrate this data freely, including in
  commercial products.
- You can adapt, extend, or remix it.
- You must give credit to NexicScript as the source.
- If you publicly redistribute this database, or a modified version of
  it, you must keep it open under this same license. You cannot take this
  data, close it off, and resell it as your own proprietary dataset. This is
  the same protection used by OpenStreetMap — it exists specifically so a
  shared database can't be taken and re-closed by someone else.
- This applies to the database itself (the compiled, structured data).
  If you build a product or app that simply uses this data internally,
  that product does not need to be open-sourced — only a redistribution of
  the database itself triggers this requirement.

The full license terms are the ones that govern — see below.

